  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s027-p00248",
      "source_en": "As discussed in the second chapter, two different chronologies have been applied for Central Saharan rock art, namely a high and a low one. According to the high chronology the earliest phases of the Round Head paintings date to the 10th millennium BP (e. g. Mori 2000; Aumassip 2004) but the low chronology places them only to the 8th-7th millennium BP (Muzzolini 1995a, b). In this chapter evidence supporting the high chronology and the Early Holocene age of the origin of Round Head art is presented, as well as an hypothesis for its evolution and the evidence for contact with other rock art producing groups.",
